    // h(){ local g=5; f; echo $g; }` prints 1). The innermost frame holding NAME loses it as
    // a whole - a name declared local twice there restores its FIRST saved value - and its
    // entries are dropped so that frame's return does not restore over later writes.
    // Answers false when no caller frame holds NAME. Twin of rt_unset_up in bash-rt.c.
    function unsetCallerLocal(name) {
