            // goes first: a "?" takes one character, and a ?(..) or *(..) group is tried right
            // there and then dropped, so *?(a) and **(a) both act as "*". What follows is tried
            // at every start BEFORE the end of the subject, never at the end itself, so
            // [[ xy == *@(|a) ]] is false - except that at the end a !(..) in the top-level
